1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,294
Sworn is for Tempo Zones.

2
00:00:02,344 --> 00:00:09,325
They keep payments private: users see only their own; only the operator sees every transaction.

3
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:14,950
So before a withdrawal, no outside reviewer can verify the private batch.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,044
Zcash uses zero knowledge to prove a transaction is valid without revealing it.

5
00:00:21,094 --> 00:00:26,200
Sworn uses it differently: it proves a Zone batch executed correctly,

6
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:29,950
without publishing transactions; the operator still sees them.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,064
Tempo Zones ship no native ZK proof today.

8
00:00:34,114 --> 00:00:40,236
We compiled Tempo's own Zone verifier for SP1, with its logic unchanged,

9
00:00:40,286 --> 00:00:47,950
bound it to the portal's batch inputs, and verified a test-fixture proof read-only on Moderato.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,223
Separately, on our own one-operator Zone, the portal settled three batches only after the proof passed;

11
00:00:55,273 --> 00:00:59,314
then our sequencer, not the proof, paid a withdrawal.

12
00:00:59,364 --> 00:01:02,950
Then our own sequencer signed a forged batch.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,950
It was rejected: a real proof cannot authorize a different batch.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,491
First buyer: a Zone business whose reviewer cannot reconstruct the witness.

15
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:20,436
One batch tests demand; repeats and upgrades become Proof Operations.

16
00:01:20,486 --> 00:01:27,572
The market grows with Zones, batches and upgrades, if Zones are adopted.

17
00:01:27,622 --> 00:01:29,950
Later, beside Tempo's TEE.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,617
I build on Tempo's stack, Reth and Revm, and teach it through Fabrknt Dojo.

19
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:39,950
Uniswap Foundation sponsor prize at ETHGlobal Tokyo;

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,617
third in Superteam Japan and NTT DOCOMO R&D's side track at Colosseum's Cypherpunk hackathon.

21
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:49,950
Before crypto, fifteen years of banking systems.

22
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,150
Today: testnet, unaudited, no customers yet.

23
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:56,883
Next, one design partner supplies a batch,

24
00:01:56,933 --> 00:02:02,750
and its reviewer decides whether the evidence is worth paying for.

25
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,950
Sworn: verifiable evidence for private execution.
